<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Feed group buys 54,000 tonnes U.S. corn.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Feed group buys 54,000 tonnes U.S. corn.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Members Feed Industry Group bought a 54,000-tonne shipment of U.S. No.2 corn from Mitsui at a spot tender on Thursday, traders said.  </p>
<p>The shipment was bought on an FOB basis and freight was fixed at US$10 per tonne, traders said.</p>
<p>The shipment was slated for delivery from the Pacific Northwest December 6-20, they said.</p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follow:</p>
<p> Shipment Tonne   Price/futures</p>
<p>	    36,000  63.74 US cents/Dec</p>
<p>	    18,000  US$148.60</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
